  "note": "This character's parts arrived as individually-positioned PNG blobs on one canvas rather than the fixed 1:1 blueprint grid, and every future character's parts will arrive the same way -- so this rig is built by reading each part at its OWN NATIVE pixel size straight off the source image (the sizes there are already correct/1:1 relative to each other; do not rescale them to fit a template) and letting build_geometry measure proportions from those native sizes directly, exactly like the existing 'folder of separately exported PNGs' load path. The automatic wrist-pivot detector (_detect_wrist_pivot, which assumes the wrist end has a WIDER cross-section than the finger end) got several of this character's hands backwards: a relaxed hand with fingers curled CLOSED (not splayed open) can be wider at the curled-finger end than at the smooth wrist dome, which is exactly backwards from that assumption. Every hand_variants pivot below was therefore set by eye against the actual art instead, per the instruction to save real per-character data rather than trust one general heuristic for every art style.",
